\begin_layout Title
Setting For RP2350 HAL
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For Alire,
 the direct equivalent of the RP2040 HAL (pico_bsp or similar local packages) is the embedded_rp2350 crate.
 It provides the necessary Ada/SPARK runtimes for the GNAT compiler targeting the RP2350's ARM Cortex-M33 architecture.For a complete development ecosystem with Alire,
 the environment consists of:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
The Runtime Environment
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To run bare-metal Ada tasks on the RP2350 Alire uses the community-bb-runtimes repository.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Standard profiles can be pulled depending on needs:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
light
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
light-tasking (for Ravenscar tasking)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
embedded.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Setting Up A Project
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To use the equivalent of the old pico_bsp structure,
 configure the <Project_Name>.gpr file to import the new board definitions and target architectures:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
with "config/hello_pico_config.gpr";
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
with "embedded_rp2350.gpr";
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
project Hello_Pico is
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for Target use "thumbv8m.main-none-eabihf";
 -- Cortex-M33 target
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for Runtime ("Ada") use "light-tasking";
 -- Or another selected profile
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for Source_Dirs use ("src/",
 "config/");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for Object_Dir use "obj";
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for Main use ("main.adb");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
package Linker is
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for Switches ("Ada") use Embedded_RP2350.Linker_Switches & ("-Wl,--gc-sections");
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
end Linker;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
end Hello_Pico;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Targeting Both ARM Cores
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Because the RP2350 boots both cores into the same architecture by default,
 utilizing Core 0 and Core 1 as ARM cores requires configuring the Ada runtime to coordinate dual-core tasking or manually booting Core 1 via the hardware registers.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
The GPR Project File Configuration
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Ensure your project file explicitly locks onto the ARMv8-M (Cortex-M33) instruction set with Hard Floating Point support (-eabihf):
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
with "config/hello_pico_config.gpr";
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
with "embedded_rp2350.gpr";
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
project Hello_Pico is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Locks the project to the ARM Cortex-M33 architecture
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for Target use "thumbv8m.main-none-eabihf";
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- "light-tasking" allows Ravenscar/Jorvik multiprocessor tasking profiles
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for Runtime ("Ada") use "light-tasking";
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for Source_Dirs use ("src/",
 "config/");
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for Object_Dir use "obj";
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for Main use ("main.adb");
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
package Linker is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for Switches ("Ada") use Embedded_RP2350.Linker_Switches & ("-Wl,--gc-sections");
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end Linker;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end Hello_Pico;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Multi-Core Execution Models in Ada
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Depending on the level of complexity you want,
 there are two primary ways to manage both ARM cores:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Option A:
 The Ravenscar / Jorvik Multiprocessor Way (Recommended)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If your light-tasking profile supports Symmetric Multiprocessing (SMP) for the RP2350 package the Ada runtime handles the second core automatically.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
You distribute tasks across the cores using the CPU aspect:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
pragma Profile (Ravenscar);
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
package Core_Tasks is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- This task will run exclusively on Core 0
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
task Core_0_Worker with
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
CPU => 1;
 -- Ada CPU IDs start at 1 (Core 0)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- This task will run exclusively on Core 1
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
task Core_1_Worker with
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
CPU => 2;
 -- (Core 1)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end Core_Tasks;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
package body Core_Tasks is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
task body Core_0_Worker is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
begin
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
loop
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Core 0 specific workload (e.g.,
 USB or Main state machine)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
null;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end loop;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end body Core_0_Worker;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
task body Core_1_Worker is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
begin
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
loop
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Core 1 specific workload (e.g.,
 PIO management or math calculations)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
null;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end loop;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end body Core_1_Worker;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
end Core_Tasks;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Option B:
 Manual Core-1 Booting (Sequential Control)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If a bare-bones implementation without the tasking runtime (light profile) is preferred Core 1 stays sleeping at boot.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Core 1 must be woken up using the RP2350's hardware control blocks.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The embedded_rp2350 or peripheral HAL libraries provide bindings to the SIO (Single-Cycle IO) block:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Clear FIFO status flags via SIO registers.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Send the wake sequence (Launch command,
 Vector Table address,
 Stack Pointer,
 and Entry Point) to Core 1's FIFO.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Core 1 wakes up directly executing your designated secondary Ada procedure.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Migrate Alire Configuration File
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To migrate an Alire configuration file (alire.toml) from the RP2040 to the RP2350 the device HAL,
 Board Support Package (BSP),
 and runtime environment packages must be swapped out for their RP2350-specific equivalents.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Assuming that the ARM cores are being used,
 amend the alire.toml file to use the code block:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
[[depends-on]]
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
rp2350_hal = "^1.0"
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
pico2_bsp = "^1.0"
\begin_inset Note Note
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
light_tasking_rp2350 = "^1.0"
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
[configuration.values]
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
rp2350_hal.Use_Startup = false
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
rp2350_hal.Interrupts = "bb_runtimes"
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
light_tasking_rp2350.Max_CPUs = 2
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
light_tasking_rp2350.Board = "rpi_pico2"
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Key Changes Made
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
rp2040_hal → rp2350_hal
\series default
 swaps the peripheral drivers for the new RP2350 architecture.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
pico_bsp → pico2_bsp
\series default
 targets the Raspberry Pi Pico 2 hardware pinout mapping instead of the original Pico.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
light_tasking_rp2040 → light_tasking_rp2350
\series default
 pulls down the light-tasking bare-metal multi-processor runtime built specifically for the ARM Cortex-M33 cores.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Board = "rpi_pico" → "rpi_pico2"
\series default
 tells the Alire configuration system to inject variables specifically tailored for the newer board layout.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Max_CPUs = 2
\series default
 is retained.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This configures the runtime to properly distribute tasks across both available Cortex-M33 cores.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Final Step
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
After saving the changes to the alire.toml file drop,
 using terminal inside the project directory run the Alire update command (alr update) to pull the new dependencies and generate updated GPR project files:
\end_layout

